 Li shares as small mechanical contributors and does not say help.zig stays attributed to jnagpaul/Dhole. It lists Wen Li among likely inheritors with 40 lines but never makes the required statement about help.zig.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives a bus factor of 3, which is a stated fail condition.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A says 79% of lines belong to inactive people, and that 668 lines (43.5%) would have no author left. The combined figure is not given as about 85%. It does mention that already-departed authors exist, but the combined figure is wrong and its numbers are inconsistent.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A does not name jnagpaul, Vincent Rischmann or mochalins as having left. It also classes Felix among the inactive people (inactive by its 365-day rule), which contradicts the ground truth.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B merges Felix's variants but reports 36% (46% excluding the table). The headline share is below 40% and only about 46% when the generated table is excluded. The ground truth is 47.2% with the table excluded, so the headline fails, though the table-excluded figure is close.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Wen Li with 26% (4% without the table) and counts the table as code. It also notes that Tobias Ek has 2 lines. It does not say help.zig stays attributed to its original authors by percentage. Wen Li is above 2.5% in the headline, so it fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives a bus factor of 2, but via Felix plus Wen Li, not jnagpaul. It states Felix's share as 36%/46%, which is below half, and says jnagpaul's last commit was in 2023. The criterion allows saying Felix alone is just under half and needs a second person. The 46% excluding the table is close enough to 47%, and it names jnagpaul as having gone quiet. This is borderline but passes.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives 36–46% as the loss and separately says 37% of lines come from people inactive. It does not combine them into about 85%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B names jnagpaul (2023), Vincent Rischmann (2025) and mochalins (2025) as quiet. It says Felix is still active. It does not credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion, and the criterion requires that credit, so it fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C reports Felix at 37% headline, about 48% without the generated table. The headline is below 40%, so it fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C credits Wen Li with 25% and treats the table as code in the headline. It does say help.zig is already someone else's code, but it does not give the shares required. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives a bus factor of about 2, but via Felix and Wen, not jnagpaul. It does not say jnagpaul stopped contributing. Felix near 50% without the table is mentioned. It does not name the second person correctly, so it fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives 37% as the loss, with no combination with departed authors.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C does not list who has left. It only says 11 people committed in the last 12 months.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D reports Felix at about 39%, below 40%, and has a tool counting him separately.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D says help.zig is 100% Tobias Ek. This is a stated fail.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives a bus factor of about 4, which is 3 or more.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives 39% and says 90% of args.zig is inactive, but it classes Felix as inactive. It gives no combined figure near 85%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D treats Felix as inactive and credits help.zig to Tobias Ek. It fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E merges four emails and reports Felix at about 37%, below 40%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E credits Wen Li with 25%, counts the table, and does not credit help.zig correctly. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives a bus factor of about 2 for the repo, but does not name jnagpaul or say they stopped contributing. Felix is stated at 37%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives 37% as the loss and says no part of the code is orphaned. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E does not name the departed authors, and says no part is orphaned.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F reports Felix at 35.8%, below 40%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Wen Li with 26% and counts the table. It also suggests Tobias Ek as a width code reviewer. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives a bus factor of 2 with Felix plus Wen Li, and says Felix is at 35.8%. It does not name jnagpaul's departure as the second person. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives 36% and 62%. It does not give about 85%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F says Felix is not active, which is a stated fail. It also does not list the departed authors correctly.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":14980,"type":"result","duration_ms":15012,"uuid":"9c59d304-83e0-4493-b4cf-92f1b934e9d2","ttft_stream_ms":2327,"time_to_request_ms":665,"first_content_frame_ms":2327,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
